er the acquired fund's operations.\n- The investment is consistent with the acquiring fund's investment objectives and policies.\n\nThe findings should be documented and reported to the acquiring fund's board, with the board's oversight of the adviser's process.\n\n**Fund of funds investment agreement:** The acquiring and acquired funds generally need a written fund of funds investment agreement. It typically addresses:\n- Acknowledgment of the rule's conditions and limits on control.\n- Voting and redemption arrangements.\n- Sales-load and fee-related terms.\n- Mechanisms for the acquired fund to reject or limit investments.\n\nBecause the precise conditions, including any board-approval and notice requirements, depend on the rule text and the specific structure, confirm them against the current Rule 12d1-4 and SEC guidance before relying on this summary.","ttft_ms":8201,"type":"result","duration_ms":9692,"uuid":"add66be9-199d-4b33-aaf6-0a6627278844","ttft_stream_ms":942,"time_to_request_ms":75,"first_content_frame_ms":942,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
